            {
                "entry_id": "b9c627a8-f792-3128-b93e-cf6b60776df8",
                "word": "pyramidiot",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f68125a6-ad29-4756-8d66-00c3bb34435a",
                        "entry_id": "b9c627a8-f792-3128-b93e-cf6b60776df8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pyramidiots"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3cc7054e-39f7-3f0d-9836-df8b363f0f87",
                        "entry_id": "b9c627a8-f792-3128-b93e-cf6b60776df8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Individu proposant ou adhérant à des théories pseudo-scientifiques ou farfelues au sujet des pyramides."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2751e46-b070-42d8-823c-b63fcc3e2c99",
                                "sense_id": "3cc7054e-39f7-3f0d-9836-df8b363f0f87",
                                "text": "En effet, c’est à Meïdoum que l’ajustage des joints montre, pour la première fois, cette finesse véritablement extraordinaire que les pyramidiots resservent à toutes les sauces."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c61eb9c-52aa-4b5b-a15c-32b846d02dc9",
                                "sense_id": "3cc7054e-39f7-3f0d-9836-df8b363f0f87",
                                "text": "oui, en fait, le nom de l’article est trompeur, ce n’est pas Batman le pyramidiot, mais bien les ignares d’auteurs qui sont suffisamment cons pour, en plus, faire du prosélytisme primaire de leur idioties."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1eb183ca-285b-472b-9b02-a09e77a23987",
                                "sense_id": "3cc7054e-39f7-3f0d-9836-df8b363f0f87",
                                "text": "Des pyramidiots, il y en a beaucoup. Beaucoup trop, diraient certaines mauvaises langues, mais sans eux, il faut bien avouer que les internets seraient encore plus calmes qu’un dimanche après-midi dunkerquois."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5b510da1-36c9-41f0-9b07-0587f70349bf",
                        "source_entry_id": "b9c627a8-f792-3128-b93e-cf6b60776df8",
                        "source_sense_id": "3cc7054e-39f7-3f0d-9836-df8b363f0f87",
                        "target_lang_word": "pyramidiot",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pyramidiot",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3065ffba-2c74-388e-8cdb-c70aeb438b5b",
                                        "entry_id": "71377f6c-e4f2-3dde-a878-1b98058d696d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "pyramidologist; one who believes prophecies are encoded in Egyptian pyramids."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2e0f00f-c97f-45da-a830-a61e2f7f3e96",
                                                "sense_id": "3065ffba-2c74-388e-8cdb-c70aeb438b5b",
                                                "text": "It has been customary in some circles to dub them ' Pyramid-ites ', but after all ' Smyrniot ' and ' Cypriot ' are used for ' those of Smyrna ' and ' those of Cyprus ', so why not Pyramidiot ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e06cf17-d141-459c-9d7f-c47f3179f58d",
                                                "sense_id": "3065ffba-2c74-388e-8cdb-c70aeb438b5b",
                                                "text": "If I started babbling about Nefertiti, they would shrug, shake their heads sadly, and write me off as some kind of pyramidiot. But if my wild tale were backed up by two responsible, respected professionals, Bloch would be in real trouble."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcdfc37d-83b9-4dce-81e0-4cffed8958d6",
                                                "sense_id": "3065ffba-2c74-388e-8cdb-c70aeb438b5b",
                                                "text": "Deverell was both a cultural diffusionist and a pyramidiot. He insisted that ancient Egypt had acquired its civilization from England, whose colony Egypt had been in ancient times."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a4efa6f-86d6-4d71-bffa-d408dea508f6",
                                                "sense_id": "3065ffba-2c74-388e-8cdb-c70aeb438b5b",
                                                "text": "Listen how a little of it looked: Wisely, somebody, probably Richard Loren, veteran Pyramidiot as well as promotor, chose to begin the first set with Hamza el-Din, an internationally famous master of the oud."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9ce633c-5dbc-47fb-ae1f-44d4d7c6eb9f",
                                                "sense_id": "3065ffba-2c74-388e-8cdb-c70aeb438b5b",
                                                "text": "His manipulations of figures had enormous appeal and his books were read by thousands, but his conclusions were debunked by scholars, who called him a \" pyramidiot.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "871d6f77-adc5-4d74-86d1-1b92ec6200ad",
                                                "sense_id": "3065ffba-2c74-388e-8cdb-c70aeb438b5b",
                                                "text": "The roots of the pyramidologist or pyramidiot probably go back to the time the pyramids were built, but their flowering arrived with the antiquarians of the 19th century."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
